          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong symmetric algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            of a vector space is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            This construction generalizes to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+representations"} group representations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear categories
            with enough
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rig"} 2-rig
          %h2#explicit_definition Explicit definition
          %p We begin with the construction for vector spaces and then sketch how to generalize it.
          %h3#for_vector_spaces For vector spaces
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %strong symmetric algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            is generated by the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            using these operations:
          %ul
            %li addition and scalar multiplication
            %li
              an associative binary operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
          %p subject to these identities:
          %ul
            %li
              the identities necessary for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
              to be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %li
              the identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %mi w
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \cdot w = w \cdot v
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
          %p
            It then follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi p
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^p V
            is spanned by
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 \cdot \cdots \cdot v_p
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, \dots, v_p \in V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            is also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative
          %p
            The symmetric algebra of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is also denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym V
            = succeed "." do
              %strong polynomial algebra
            %em in
            the elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            %em on
            the vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(V^*)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fock+space"} Fock space
          %h3#in_general In general
          %p
            More generally, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in C
            is any object. Then we can form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor powers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has countable coproducts we can form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T V = \bigoplus_{n \ge 0} V^{\otimes n}
          %p
            (which we write here as a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T V
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            object in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi p
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi q
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes p} \otimes V^{\otimes q} \to V^{\otimes (p+q)}
          %p
            This monoid object is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            acts on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear category
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            zero, then we can form the symmetrization map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A : V^{\otimes n} \to V^{\otimes n}
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A = \frac{1}{n!} \sum_{\sigma \in S_n} \sigma
          %p
            This is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            we can form its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %strong symmetric tensor power
            or
            %strong symmetric power
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n V
            (e.g
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gallier11"} Gallier 2011, p. 27
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V = \bigoplus_{n \ge 0} S^n V
          %p
            becomes a monoid object called the
            %strong symmetric algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a more general sort of symmetric monoidal category, then we need a different construction of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a symmetric monoidal category with finite colimits, we can simply define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n V
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of the action of the symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            also has countable coproducts, we can define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V = \coprod_{n \ge 0} S^n V
          %p
            Then, if the tensor product distributes over these colimits (as in a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rig"} 2-rig
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V
            will become a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} commutative monoid object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em free
            commutative monoid object on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to A \, ,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a commutative monoid, factors uniquely as the obvious morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to S V
          %p followed by a morphism of commutative monoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S V \to A  \, ,
          %p as in this commutative triangle:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mi V
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  \&amp;          &amp; S V \\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp;                 &amp; \searrow \\
                  V &amp;          &amp; \longrightarrow &amp;          &amp; A
                  }
          %h3#in_even_more_generality In even more generality
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is an object in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon-enriched+symmetric+monoidal+category"} CMon-enriched symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            such that the following diagram admits a joint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
